  "hard_rules": [
    "Every episode has at least two non-empty source records and at least one PRE_OR_AT_CUTOFF source supporting first negative evidence or a formal counterexample.",
    "POST_CUTOFF sources may support evaluator-side successor/history only and may never support candidate-visible pre-cutoff replay.",
    "Every episode has at least two alternative interpretations unless the exact formal counterexample relation makes historical causal interpretation irrelevant; even then interpretation alternatives must cover scope/preservation.",
    "private_cognition is always CANNOT_INFER.",
    "historical_use is always MECHANISM_EXTRACTION_ONLY and protected_confirmatory_gold is always false.",
    "DECISIVE_FOR_REGISTERED_CLAIM must name non-empty excluded_scope_ids and may not imply a broader global prohibition.",
    "NONDECISIVE, RESPONSIBILITY_UNRESOLVED and EXECUTION_OR_MEASUREMENT_INVALIDATES_REFUTATION may not manufacture excluded_scope_ids beyond a registered method/interface/measurement defect.",
    "Every episode names still-live alternatives or explicitly records NONE_AFTER_EXACT_FORMAL_REFUTATION for the exact quantified claim.",
    "Preserved successes must remain explicit when a proof, model, method, interface or theory survives in a narrower domain.",
    "A changed-context retry is not a contradiction of prior negative knowledge; changes_context is stored on each patch/replication record.",
    "Same-symptom paired cases may share outcome class but must be allowed different responsibility hypotheses/resolution classes.",
    "No row may set independent_domain_expert_review_status to OBTAINED_AGREEMENT without an attached external review record.",
    "The corpus-ready terminal is forbidden while independent expert agreement is absent."
  ],
